[[File:Woodcutting node in Daemonheim.png|thumb|An entgallow tree found in Daemonheim]]
'''Woodcutting''' in [[Daemonheim]] is accessible to [[Free-to-play]] and [[Pay-to-play]]. It can be used to open skill doors and cut trees grown in the dungeons.

To cut trees, players must be delving a dungeon with high complexity.

==Opening doors==
[[File:Woodcutting door.png|thumb|right|151px|A door requiring woodcutting to be opened.]]
Woodcutting in Dungeoneering allows players to clear [[wooden barricade]]s on certain doors found throughout the dungeons. The highest level required to open a door is level 105. All doors in the main path are unlockable by at least one player in the team. Failure to clear barricades on doors will cause sharp debris from door to drop and deal large damage to the player making the attempt.

==Hatchets==
The player may use a hatchet if they have the Woodcutting level to do so. Hatchets may be purchased from the smuggler, smithed at an anvil, or dropped by monsters.

